# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change to the paths that can hurt someone else.
#
# Deliberately NO `*` default: reports, suites and knowledge files are high-volume and need only the
# ordinary one approval from anyone. Ownership is reserved for paths where a wrong change ships to
# plugin users, weakens a containment boundary, or silently disables a gate.
#
# Rules: the LAST matching line wins, so specific paths come after general ones. Every line names at
# least TWO owners — an author cannot approve their own PR, so a sole owner blocks their own work.
# An owner without write access is ignored by GitHub; check the "CODEOWNERS errors" view after edits.

# CI, workflows and this file itself.
